# MovieInator local live-run configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (already git-ignored, see .gitignore) and fill in the
# operator-supplied values marked below. Never commit `.env.local` or any real secret value.
# This file is safe to commit: every value here is a placeholder or a non-secret default.
#
# Load path: `npm run start:google` sources `.env.local` automatically. `npm run google:preflight`
# also sources it (see scripts/google-preflight.js / package.json). No other script or test reads
# this file; `npm test` and `npm run check` remain network-free and credential-free regardless of
# what is in `.env.local`.
#
# Full walkthrough: docs/operator-runbook.md (Part A: enable one live Gemini REST call).

# --- Operator must supply these four values ---
# Your Google Cloud project ID (Vertex AI must have aiplatform.googleapis.com enabled on it).
GOOGLE_PROJECT_ID=
# The Vertex AI region for your model, e.g. us-central1, or "global".
GOOGLE_LOCATION=
# The exact Vertex AI model ID you have access to, e.g. gemini-2.0-flash-001.
GOOGLE_MODEL_ID=
# Your Parallel Search API key from https://platform.parallel.ai (optional feature, see Part C
# of docs/operator-runbook.md). Leave blank to keep external evidence enrichment disabled.
PARALLEL_API_KEY=

# --- Runtime mode: local ADC-backed live Gemini call path ---
RUNTIME_MODE=adc_local
DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=local
MODEL_BACKEND=google_rest
GOOGLE_GEMINI_ENABLED=true
GOOGLE_PUBLISHER=google
GOOGLE_REST_API_VERSION=v1
GOOGLE_AUTH_MODE=adc
AGENT_RUNTIME_MODE=local_mock

# --- Parallel Search enrichment (bounded, off unless PARALLEL_API_KEY above is set) ---
PARALLEL_ENABLED=true
PARALLEL_SEARCH_MODE=advanced
PARALLEL_TIMEOUT_MS=8000
PARALLEL_MAX_TOPICS=2
PARALLEL_MAX_RESULTS_PER_TOPIC=3

# --- Do not set these ---
# GOOGLE_GEMINI_READINESS is informational only: src/gemini-rest.js never reads it as authority.
# Only a real, passed, unstale GeminiReadiness.check() result (npm run google:preflight, then the
# server's own boot-time preflight) makes the server report or use a live call path. Setting this
# variable to "passed" here does nothing and cannot fake liveness.
#
# GOOGLE_SDK_VERSION is read into config but not otherwise used by any call path; leave it unset.
